---
import WorkbenchLayout from "../../../layouts/WorkbenchLayout.astro";
---

<WorkbenchLayout
  title="AI Field Training | PENGO Workbench"
  description="Training materials for using the PENGO Workbench to inspect AI outputs, prompts, workflow failures, and structural gaps."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/workbench/aift/"
  active="training"
  breadcrumb="AI Field Training"
>
  <article class="wb-content wb-template">
    <p class="wb-type-label">Training</p>
    <h1>AI Field Training</h1>
    <p class="wb-lede">
      Practical training for using the Workbench to inspect AI-facing failures, input gaps, and structural patterns.
    </p>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        AI Field Training is the training layer for the Workbench. It will turn Issues,
        Patterns, Lenses, Check Input, and Explore Results into guided practice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Training pages may explain how to inspect an AI ask, read mapped Workbench
        references, compare structural failure surfaces, and avoid treating every
        bad result as a model failure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Planned Training Types</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Check Input walkthroughs</li>
        <li>Explore Results practice examples</li>
        <li>Issue-to-Pattern reading exercises</li>
        <li>Pattern and Lens interpretation drills</li>
        <li>AI-adjacent failure triage examples</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>How to Read This</h2>
      <p>
        AI Field Training is instructional material. It does not define canonical
        Issues, Patterns, Lenses, Categories, or validation rules.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</WorkbenchLayout>
